From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:14:13 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] info pages: no Apply/Reset/Defaults footer

The pages only show command output; there is nothing to apply. KCM buttons set to NoAdditionalButton (about-distro does the
same); the default footer showed Defaults / Reset / Apply in System Settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
---
 src/qml/CommandOutputKCM.qml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/qml/CommandOutputKCM.qml b/src/qml/CommandOutputKCM.qml
index c0f1da5..22fde48 100644
--- a/src/qml/CommandOutputKCM.qml
+++ b/src/qml/CommandOutputKCM.qml
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@ import org.kde.kinfocenter.private as Private
 KCM.AbstractKCM {
     id: root
 
+    // read-only information: nothing to apply, reset or restore (System Settings would show Defaults/Reset/Apply)
+    KCM.ConfigModule.buttons: KCM.ConfigModule.NoAdditionalButton
+
     implicitWidth: Kirigami.Units.gridUnit * 20
     implicitHeight: Kirigami.Units.gridUnit * 20
 
